NOTE: It's a mod loader, NOT a mod! Install this pack only if another mod requires BepInEx, or if you are developing a BepInEx mod.

[size=4][b]What this is[/b][/size]
BepInEx is a mod loader for The Last Plague: Blight. Install this pack if a mod lists it as a requirement.

This pack contains the official BepInEx build [url=https://builds.bepinex.dev/projects/bepinex_be][b]6.0.0-be.793[/b][/url] ([font=Courier New]BepInEx-Unity.IL2CPP-win-x64-6.0.0-be.793+dbc82f0.zip[/font]) with its original files unchanged. Tested with The Last Plague: Blight v0.12.7.

[b]This pack is unofficial.[/b] The developer of The Last Plague: Blight does not make, support, or endorse it. The BepInEx team does not endorse this pack either.

[size=4][b]Install[/b][/size]
Close the game. Download the zip from the Files tab using Manual download.
[list=1]
[*]Extract the zip into [font=Courier New]C:\Program Files (x86)\Steam\steamapps\common\The Last Plague[/font] [i](if you installed Steam or the game elsewhere, find the folder in your Steam Library: right-click The Last Plague: Blight > Manage > Browse local files)[/i].[/*]
[*]Start the game from Steam. Wait for the main menu, then quit before installing mods.[/*]
[/list]

Example after extraction (other game files omitted):
[code]C:\Program Files (x86)\Steam\steamapps\common\The Last Plague\
├── BepInEx\
├── dotnet\
├── TheLastPlague.exe
├── doorstop_config.ini
└── winhttp.dll[/code]

[size=4][b]The first start[/b][/size]
[list]
[*]An internet connection is required for the initial setup. BepInEx downloads the Unity libraries of the game (about 1.7 MB) from the BepInEx site.[/*]
[*]BepInEx prepares files for mods before the game opens. The first start took about 20 seconds longer on my PC. Wait for the main menu.[/*]
[*]The BepInEx console window opens with the game. [b]Do not close the console window[/b], because that also closes the game.[/*]
[/list]
Check that the console shows [font=Courier New]BepInEx 6.0.0-be.793 - TheLastPlague[/font].

Mods go into [font=Courier New]BepInEx\plugins[/font]. Follow each mod's installation instructions.

[size=4][b]Problems[/b][/size]
[list]
[*][b]No console window opens.[/b] Check that [font=Courier New]winhttp.dll[/font] is next to [font=Courier New]TheLastPlague.exe[/font]. If the zip extracted into an extra folder, move its contents into the game folder.[/*]
[*][b]The first start stays at "Downloading unity base libraries", or the console shows "End of Central Directory record could not be found".[/b] The game could not download the Unity libraries from the BepInEx site, and no mod loads. Starting the game again does not fix it: BepInEx keeps the broken download and tries it again at each start. To fix it:[list=1]
[*]Close the game.[/*]
[*]Download [font=Courier New]Unity libraries 2021.3.45[/font] from the [url=https://www.nexusmods.com/thelastplagueblight/mods/9?tab=files]Nexus optional files[/url]. Mirrors: [url=https://unity.bepinex.dev/libraries/2021.3.45.zip]BepInEx site[/url], [url=https://github.com/ivmakk-tlpb/tlpb-bepinex-pack/releases/latest/download/2021.3.45.zip]GitHub[/url].[/*]
[*]Rename the file to exactly [font=Courier New]2021.3.45.zip[/font]. The Nexus download has a longer name, with the mod id, the version, and a date after [font=Courier New]Unity libraries 2021.3.45[/font].[/*]
[*]Do not extract it. Put the zip itself into [font=Courier New]BepInEx\unity-libs[/font] in the game folder, and replace the existing file. Full path example:
[code]C:\Program Files (x86)\Steam\steamapps\common\The Last Plague\BepInEx\unity-libs\2021.3.45.zip[/code][/*]
[*]Start the game.[/*][/list][/*]
[*][b]BepInEx is already installed.[/b] If the console shows [font=Courier New]6.0.0-be.793[/font], you do not need this pack. For a different build, follow the [url=https://github.com/ivmakk-tlpb/tlpb-bepinex-pack#replace-an-existing-installation]replacement instructions[/url].[/*]
[*][b]My antivirus warns about winhttp.dll.[/b] This file loads BepInEx. It is unchanged from the official build. See [url=https://github.com/ivmakk-tlpb/tlpb-bepinex-pack#verify-the-download]how to compare the files with the official download[/url].[/*]
[*][b]Mods stopped working after a game update.[/b] Check this page and your mods' pages for updates. To play without mods, follow the Uninstall steps below.[/*]
[*][b]The game does not start.[/b] Follow the Uninstall steps below. Then, in Steam, select Properties > Installed Files > Verify integrity of game files.[/*]
[/list]
Before reporting a game bug to the developer, check whether it still happens without mods.

[size=4][b]Uninstall[/b][/size]
Close the game. To keep your mods and settings, copy [font=Courier New]BepInEx\plugins[/font] and [font=Courier New]BepInEx\config[/font] somewhere outside the game folder.

Delete these files and entire folders from the game folder:
[code]BepInEx/
dotnet/
.doorstop_version
changelog.txt
doorstop_config.ini
winhttp.dll[/code]
Deleting [font=Courier New]BepInEx[/font] removes all installed mods and their settings. Keep the game folder and all other files. The game then runs without mods. These steps do not delete your save files.

[size=4][b]Credits and more information[/b][/size]
BepInEx is made by the [url=https://github.com/BepInEx/BepInEx]BepInEx team[/url] and contributors and is licensed under LGPL-2.1. Credits and license text are included in the pack.

All official BepInEx builds, this one ([url=https://builds.bepinex.dev/projects/bepinex_be/793/BepInEx-Unity.IL2CPP-win-x64-6.0.0-be.793%2Bdbc82f0.zip]#793[/url]) and newer ones, are listed at [url=https://builds.bepinex.dev/projects/bepinex_be]builds.bepinex.dev[/url]. A newer build is not tested with this game until this pack moves to it.

See GitHub for [url=https://github.com/ivmakk-tlpb/tlpb-bepinex-pack#manual-install-advanced]manual installation[/url], [url=https://github.com/ivmakk-tlpb/tlpb-bepinex-pack#verify-the-download]file verification[/url], and [url=https://github.com/ivmakk-tlpb/tlpb-bepinex-pack#test-record]build test results[/url].
